    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d205">

                <pb facs="0172" n="160" xml:id="pg160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.20 Defense/34<hi rendition="#superscript"
                        >6/12</hi>: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-13T10:00:00-05:00">July 13, 1940—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>100. Department’s circular telegram of July 11, 4 p.m.<anchor n="22"
                        xml:id="d205-f1"/> The Minister for Foreign Affairs stated that he was in
                    accord with holding staff talks immediately after the Habana Conference and
                    expressed the hope that the conversations might be held at Lima.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
